  "notes": "From the official Notice of Election (Auditor Megan Reffett, dated Oct 14, 2026), linked as 'Election Public Notice' on the county election page (hosted on the county's cap.gmdsolutions.com document system). Supervisors: a single county-wide 'Vote for no more than Two' contest (at-large; no districts shown). Parties as printed: Jackson Summers (Ind), Lynn Goodrich (MAGA); Barrett White and Sarah Delanty printed with no party. Township trustees vote for no more than two, clerks one; empty candidate lists = 'No Candidate' (write-in only). No county hospital trustee contest. The notice header mentions a 'public measure', but the only measure listed is statewide Constitutional Amendment 1 (already covered); no local measure text appears. Per-precinct sample ballots were not found on the county site."
}